%   brass in the same bars: unmarked, each dotted minim was a separate tongued attack on the downbeats of 102 and 104, where the hemiola minims are tied over
%   (Adler I PDF 321: 'as in all wind and brass instruments, all slurred notes are performed on one breath, while all separate notes are tongued'; PDF 309: hard and soft
%   tonguing must be told apart in the notation; Ex. X-15, X-16 PDF 306-307). Pitches and dynamics unchanged.
