% c077: 92-94 the retransition's second head entry goes to Ob 1 (Vln II rests): the entries now pass viola -> oboe -> violins, as Beethoven 9/ii's ritmo di tre battute
%   (bars 177-195) passes its head between bassoons, oboes, clarinets and flutes over string punctuation (Adler PDF 253-255: gestures thrown between winds and strings,
%   the third time altered; PDF 271: imitation between winds and strings). The reprise retransition 241-252 keeps its all-string entries.
% c184: 101-104 the oboes hold a third, Ob 1 F sharp 5 (unison with Fl 2) over Ob 2 D sharp 5 (was Ob 1 D sharp 5 over Ob 2 on Vln II's hemiola line B4-A4-F sharp 4-D sharp 5-B4-A4, a tritone A4/D sharp 5 on
%   four of the twelve beats, at f-ff). Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 90 rule 4: concords, not discords, to two instruments of one colour, specially the oboe; PDF 52: one wind added to a string section in unison only thickens it, its colour is lost;
%   PDF 91b: one colour for the stationary parts, another for the moving ones; PDF 95: mixed unison doublings (Fl 2 + Ob 1). Ob 2's D sharp 5 still covers Tpt 1's D sharp 5 at 104 (PDF 51-52: the wood-wind softens the brass). Also 301-304 (dB).
