% c101: 101-104 Vln II plays the hemiola melody an octave under Vln I (B4-A4-F sharp 4-D sharp 5-B4-A4), with Ob 2; its old line F sharp 5/D sharp 5 is held by Fl 2 and Ob 1
%   (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 58-59: high violin melody doubled in octaves for fulness and firmness; PDF 62 Note I: melodies above the middle of the 5th octave are doubled an octave below).
% c237: 99-100 Vln II arpeggios rise (dis' fis' a', was b' fis' dis' | a' fis' dis'): they fell with Vln I in the same crotchets, and at 100 doubled its a'' fis'' dis'' an octave lower,
%   so the accompaniment merged into the line one bar before the hemiola's planned octave doubling (101), in the middle of the three-bar group 98-100.
%   Adler II PDF 217 (Ravel, Petit Poucet: melody and accompaniment in the same values need contrast to stay apart), PDF 228 (Stravinsky: colour changes without breaking up a phrase), PDF 229 (same-colour doubling swallows the line). Vla B pedal, timpani and pizz. unchanged.
