% c047: 73-77, 84, 87-88 the pp wind chord re-voiced (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 108: bassoon set inside the horns, horns on the stationary concords;
%   no fifths Hn 4/Bsn 1 F-C -> G-D at 74-75; four real parts at 77, 84, 87-88, where Hn 3 or Hn 4 doubled Bsn 1). 78-83 unchanged (Hn 3 D-D flat-C, c042).
% c045: 86-87 Cl 1 diminuendo to pp where Cl 2 enters pp on the shared staff (one printed dynamic must serve both players; Cl 1 was still p).
% c045: the harp's pedal setting at 73 printed below the LH staff: between the staves the harp's barline ran through it (MOLA PDF 8, Example 7: no collisions).
% c127: 87-88 Cl 2 D sharp 3 - C sharp 3 (was D sharp 4 - C sharp 4): the held D sharp 4 lay a third under Cl 1's F sharp 4 and met its D sharp 4 at the unison on beat 3,
%   and the C sharp 4 sat under its last note E4, so the dolce solo ended inside its own second player (Adler II PDF 267: no colour competition for a wind solo;
%   PDF 274: keep the accompaniment registrally distant, especially from woodwind solos; c027 cleared the harp from the same solo at 81-84). Chords unchanged.
% c112: 82-83 harp RH holds the dyad Bb3-D4, the common tones of the falling-third step IV-ii in F (A-S Ex. 11-2, PDF 163-164); removes the 5ths Bb3-F4 -> G3-D4 over Bb-G. Voicing only: F stays in the tune, G in harp LH and Bass Cl; harmony and the F-major episode unchanged.
% c132: 79-80 Hn 4 G3 rises to A3 (was G3-F3): over vii°7 of F the d5 G3-D flat 4 (Hn 4/Hn 3) no longer moves in similar motion to the P5 F3-C4;
%   2 rises to 3 and the tonic has a doubled 3rd (Aldwell-Schachter PDF 375, Ex. 22-3a good, 22-3c avoid). Harp LH 79 drops its G3 (<e bes>), so the
%   harp's G3-F3 does not make the same fifths a beat later against Hn 3.
% c132: 85-88 Hn 3 keeps the common tone C4 into the D sharp °7 at 87 and takes it to C sharp 4 at 88; Bsn 1 keeps the common tone A3 and falls to G3
%   (were Hn 3 C4-A3-G3, Bsn 1 A3-C4-C sharp 4: the 7th of the °7 entered by a leap in the bassoon while the horn that held it left it). Same pitches in
%   every chord (Aldwell-Schachter PDF 377-378, Ex. 22-7a-c: from IV, II or VI the 7th of °7 is prepared as a common tone; here from the N6).
